{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nInert-config class (281f, 9d7a family): a typed schema field ships with zero cfg.<section>.<field> read sites outside schema/config plumbing, so the knob silently does nothing. Env vars are already covered by the docs/env-vars.md drift gate; schema fields have no equivalent.\n\n## Approach\nDeterministic AST-level check: for each field in _config_schema.py, require >=1 attribute-read site outside the schema/config plumbing modules.\n\nDetection shape (decisive, receiver-agnostic): an ast.Attribute node in Load context whose terminal attribute name equals the field name — matching ONLY on the final `.field` segment, never on a receiver spelling. This deliberately matches every real read shape in src/: `load_config().mcp.readonly`, `config.load_config(root).verify.overlap_enabled`, a section object bound to a local (`mcp_cfg.auth_introspection_endpoint`), `self.config.<section>.<field>`, or any alias. Trade-off, stated openly: terminal-name matching is permissive — an unrelated object's same-named attribute also counts, silently keeping the gate quiet. That failure mode is fail-QUIET (a rare shadowed name suppresses a firing), never a false fire on a live field; zero-reference firing stays sound because a field with literally no `.field` attribute read anywhere cannot be read. Same-named-field collisions across sections are likewise fail-quiet and accepted. Dynamic reads (getattr dispatch) are invisible to the AST walk by design — that is exactly what the marker is for. Escape hatch: '# read-via: <path-or-reason>' comment on the field for indirect reads (getattr dispatch, client-project-only knobs) — pointer required, not a bare boolean. Fires ONLY on zero references (the bug condition), so refactors that move reads cannot FP. Failing message teaches the escape and cites in-file examples. Wire into CI alongside existing gates.\n\n## Scope\n- new check script (AST walk over src/rebar) + CI wiring\n- '# read-via:' markers for any legitimately indirect current fields (enumerate at implementation; expected small)\n\n## Testing\nUnit: field with a read passes; field with zero reads fails naming the field; read-via marker with pointer passes; marker without pointer fails. Full-tree run clean at merge.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] CI fails when any schema field has zero read sites and no read-via marker; message teaches remediation.\n- [ ] Marker requires a pointer/reason; bare markers rejected.\n- [ ] Zero-reference-only firing (no change-detector behavior on refactors).\n- [ ] Tree clean at landing with justified markers only."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785721090725465001,"uuid":"e8c7cdc5-d280-4b69-9d32-9def6c7c78e4"}